.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-CREATE-BUCKET 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-create-bucket \- create a new storage bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm create-bucket
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new storage bucket with the given name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the bucket to create. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The bucket was created; its ERN and other metadata are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or a bucket
with that name already exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm create-bucket \e
    --name reports
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-buckets (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-ern (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-bucket (1)
